Tags allow you to organize your container images. This gives you the possibility of sorting and filtering your images in any organizational pattern of your choice, which in turn helps you arrange, control and monitor your cloud resources. You can assign as many tags as you want to each image.

USAGE:
  scw registry tag <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  delete      Delete a tag
  get         Get a tag
  list        List tags

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for tag
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw registry tag [command] --help" for more information about a command.
